mpt_tokens": 7853, "total_tokens": 7853}}, "input": {"input": ["# SAP BTP Cloud Foundry Environment Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of the SAP BTP Cloud Foundry environment, highlighting key components, their relationships, and significant updates. The information is relevant to the environment's operations as of 2025.\n\n## Cloud Foundry API v2 Deprecation and Removal\n\nThe Cloud Foundry API v2 is deprecated and will be removed in the first quarter of 2026. Users must migrate to the Cloud Foundry API v3 by then. The API v3 provides improved security and performance features. The deprecation and removal of API v2 are part of SAP's efforts to maintain a secure and up-to-date platform for its customers. [Data: Sources (195, 873), Date_Range ((2022, 07, 14), (2025, 05, 15))]\n\n## Root Certificate Replacement in the SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Environment\n\nThe root certificate authority (CA) used to issue certificates on SAP domains for the SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry environment will be replaced by a newer CA. The old CA, 'DigiCert Global Root CA G2', will be replaced by 'DigiCert TLS RSA4096 Root G5'. Customers must add the new CA certificate to their trust store to ensure a seamless transition. The replacement is part of SAP's efforts to maintain a secure environment. [Data: Sources (872, 959), Date_Range ((2025, 02, 18), (2025, 06, 26))]\n\n## Cloud Logging Enhancements\n\nCloud Logging has been enhanced with new features, including the ability to load existing configuration during instance update and support for monitoring security recommendations. These enhancements improve the logging and monitoring capabilities of the Cloud Foundry environment, enabling better security and compliance. [Data: Sources (874, 875), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 15), (2025, 05, 15))]\n\n## Feature Flags Service Updates\n\nThe Feature Flags Service has been updated with new features, including a user interface upgrade to SAP Fiori, Horizon, and the ability to share service instances between different Cloud Foundry organizations. These updates improve the usability and functionality of the service, enabling better application development and deployment. [Data: Sources (876, 877), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 07), (2025, 05, 15))]\n\n## Object Store Updates\n\nThe Object Store has been updated with new features, including changes in instance deletion behavior and the revocation of AWS: S3 specific permissions for versioning and expiration rules configurations. These updates improve the storage and management capabilities of the Object Store, enabling better data security and compliance. [Data: Sources (3677, 3678), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 10), (2025, 05, 06))]\n\n## Istio Updates\n\nIstio has been updated with new features, including a compatibility version that applies new parameter sets to false and deprecates certain features. These updates improve the security and performance capabilities of Istio, enabling better network security and compliance. [Data: Sources (519, 959), Date_Range ((2025, 04, 18), (2025, 05, 06))]", "# SAP BTP Technology Overview as of May 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP BTP's key technology components, highlighting their relationships and significance within the organizational framework. The information is relevant to the company's operations around mid-2025.\n\n## Cloud Foundry API v2 Deprecation and Removal\n\nThe Cloud Foundry API v2 is deprecated and will be removed in the first quarter of 2026. This change requires users to migrate to Cloud Foundry API v3, which is the recommended version. The migration process involves updating the Cloud Foundry command line interface (CF CLI) to version 8 and updating the MultiApps CF CLI Plugin to the newest version. This change is crucial for ensuring continued service quality and operational stability. [Data: Sources (195), Date_Range ((2022, 07, 14), (2025, 05, 15))]\n\n## Root Certificate Replacement in the SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Environment\n\nThe root certificate authority (CA) used to issue certificates on SAP domains for the SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry environment needs to be changed. The old CA 'DigiCert Global Root CA G2' will be replaced by the newer 'DigiCert TLS RSA4096 Root G5'. Clients of applications offered by SAP and of those operated by customers must add the new CA certificate to their trust store to ensure a seamless transition. This change is required for maintaining the security and integrity of the SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry environment. [Data: Sources (872), Date_Range ((2025, 02, 18), (2025, 05, 15))]\n\n## Dynamic Expression Playground\n\nThe Expression Playground of SAP Automation Pilot allows users to test and debug dynamic expressions before using them in commands. This feature provides a convenient way to test how expressions will function during execution, ensuring that commands are executed correctly and efficiently. [Data: Sources (873), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 15), (2025, 05, 15))]\n\n## Loading of Existing Configuration during Instance Update\n\nCloud Logging enables loading of existing configuration during instance update via cockpit. This feature allows users to update their instance configuration without losing existing settings, ensuring that their logging configuration remains consistent and accurate. [Data: Sources (874), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 15), (2025, 05, 15))]\n\n## Support for Monitoring Security Recommendations\n\nCloud Logging service now supports Monitoring Security Recommendations with SAP Cloud ALM. This feature provides users with a comprehensive view of their security posture, enabling them to identify and address potential security risks proactively. [Data: Sources (875), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 15), (2025, 05, 15))]\n\n## SAP Fiori Horizon theme\n\nThe user interface of Feature Flags Dashboard is now upgraded to SAP Fiori, Horizon. This change provides a modern and intuitive user experience, making it easier for users to navigate and interact with the dashboard. [Data: Sources (876), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 07), (2025, 05, 15))]\n\n## Service Instance Sharing\n\nYou can now share SAP Feature Flags service instances between different Cloud Foundry organizations in the same subaccount. This feature enables users to share service instances across different organizations, streamlining their workflow and improving collaboration. [Data: Sources (877), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 15), (2025, 05, 15))]", "# SAP BTP Technology Overview as of August 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP BTP's key technology components, focusing on their relationships, operational scope, and significant updates. The information is relevant to SAP BTP's operations around mid-2025.\n\n## Automation Pilot Operational Scope\n\nThe Automation Pilot at SAP BTP plays a pivotal role in automating business processes and workflows. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2025, helps safeguard SAP BTP against potential operational pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective automation not only prevents operational anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (213, 214, 215, 216, 217), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 08, 21))]\n\n## Feature Flags Service Updates\n\nThe Feature Flags Service at SAP BTP ensures that all features are properly configured and managed. Their focus on adding new features and improving existing ones, noted starting mid-2025, is crucial in maintaining SAP BTP's reputation and operational efficiency, especially in managing complex features and business scenarios. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high standards and innovative practices. [Data: Sources (218, 219, 220, 221, 222), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 07), (2025, 08, 21))]\n\n## Cloud Logging and Security Enhancements\n\nCloud Logging at SAP BTP ensures that all logging and monitoring activities are properly configured and managed. Their focus on adding new features and improving existing ones, noted starting mid-2025, is crucial in maintaining SAP BTP's reputation and operational efficiency, especially in managing complex logging and monitoring scenarios. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high standards and innovative practices. [Data: Sources (223, 224, 225, 226, 227), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 15), (2025, 08, 21))]", "# SAP BTP Cloud Foundry Runtime Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of the SAP BTP Cloud Foundry Runtime, highlighting key components, their relationships, and significant updates. The information is relevant to the SAP BTP Cloud Foundry Runtime's operations as of 2025.\n\n## Cloud Foundry API v2 Deprecation and Removal\n\nThe Cloud Foundry API v2 is deprecated and replaced by the Cloud Foundry API v3. The usage of the Cloud Foundry API v2 is restricted by rate limits, which will decrease over time and eventually reach zero in the first quarter of 2026. It is essential to migrate any direct usage of CF API v2 to CF API v3. [Data: Sources (195, 877), Date_Range ((2022, 07, 14), (2026, 01, 01))]\n\n## Root Certificate Replacement in the SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Environment\n\nThe root certificate authority (CA) used to issue the certificates on SAP domains for the SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry environment needs to be changed. The old CA 'DigiCert Global Root CA G2' will be replaced by the newer 'DigiCert TLS RSA4096 Root G5'. Clients of applications offered by SAP and of those operated by customers must add the new CA certificate to their trust store in order to ensure a seamless transition. [Data: Sources (872), Date_Range ((2025, 02, 18), (2025, 06, 30))]\n\n## Dynamic Expression Playground\n\nThe Expression Playground of SAP Automation Pilot allows users to test and debug dynamic expressions before using them in their commands. The playground also gives users the option to load commands that are prepopulated with sample values, which allows them to test how the expressions will function during execution. [Data: Sources (873), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 15), (2025, 05, 15))]", "# SAP Cloud Foundry and SAP BTP Overview as of July 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of key components and services within SAP Cloud Foundry and SAP BTP, highlighting their interactions and updates as of July 2025. The information is relevant to the company's operations and technology advancements during this period.\n\n## Cloud Foundry Readiness Health Checks\n\nStarting at the end of September 2025, MTA deployment in Cloud Foundry will support Cloud Foundry readiness health checks by introducing new module-specific parameters. Users may encounter problems during MTA deployment if the parameters are already defined in their MTA descriptor but are incorrectly configured. In such cases, the MTA deployments will start to fail with the error message: None of the instances of the app become routable. Please verify that the defined MTA parameters for the readiness health check align with the app's code and configuration. [Data: Sources (765), Date_Range ((2025, 09, 01), (2025, 09, 30))]\n\n## Java Server Updates\n\nJava Web Tomcat 10 (runtime version 5.26) has been updated to Tomcat version 10.1.42, and Java Web Tomcat 9 (runtime version 4.106) and Java EE 7 Web Profile TomEE 7 (runtime version 1.204) have been updated to Tomcat version 9.0.106. Recommended action: Update your applications to the latest runtime version. [Data: Sources (473, 474), Date_Range ((2025, 07, 01), (2025, 07, 10))]\n\n## Automation Pilot Enhancements\n\nYou can now use commands for management of transport nodes, routes, and transport requests in SAP Cloud Transport Management. Additionally, you can use your existing Cloud Connector setup to interact with systems that are not directly accessible from the public Internet. [Data: Sources (475, 476), Date_Range ((2025, 07, 01), (2025, 07, 10))]\n\n## Cloud Logging Upgrade\n\nCloud Logging offers a major version upgrade of underlying OpenSearch towards version 2.19. This brings major advancements and new features. The upgrade can be explored immediately, within 3 months a mandatory migration will be rolled out. [Data: Sources (478), Date_Range ((2025, 07, 01), (2025, 07, 10))]\n\n## SAP BTP Cockpit Enhancements\n\nWe've extended our recently released budgeting feature, currently in beta testing, to now support the Pay-As-You-Go for SAP BTP flavor of the consumption-based commercial model. [Data: Sources (479), Date_Range ((2025, 07, 01), (2025, 07, 10))]\n\n## Cloud Portal Service Updates\n\nThe Key User Adaptation site setting is enabled by default for new sites. [Data: Sources (480), Date_Range ((2025, 07, 01), (2025, 07, 03))]", "# SAP Cloud Foundry and Kyma Environment Overview as of August 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of the SAP Cloud Foundry and Kyma environment, highlighting key components, their relationships, and significant updates. The information is relevant to the SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry environment and its users.\n\n## SAP Java Buildpack Deprecation\n\nThe SAP Java Buildpack 1 has been deprecated and will be removed from the SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry environment in June 2025. This change is part of the company's efforts to focus on delivering highly-requested new features, reducing technical debt, and boosting product quality and security. Users are required to migrate their applications to SAP Java Buildpack 2 as soon as possible to avoid any disruptions. [Data: Sources (224), Date_Range ((2024, 08, 16), (2024, 08, 22))]\n\n## API Gateway Module Update\n\nThe API Gateway module has been updated to version 2.5.0, which includes support for request modifiers in the v2alpha1 APIRule custom resource. This change is part of the company's efforts to improve the security and scalability of the API Gateway module. Users are advised to review the updated documentation for more information. [Data: Sources (2369), Date_Range ((2024, 08, 08), (2024, 08, 22))]\n\n## Object Store Updates\n\nThe Object Store has been updated to support blob index match on Azure. This change is part of the company's efforts to improve the security and scalability of the Object Store. Users are advised to review the updated documentation for more information. [Data: Sources (2370), Date_Range ((2024, 08, 22), (2024, 08, 22))]\n\n## Resource Groups Limit\n\nThe maximum number of resource groups is limited at tenant level to 50. If users reach this limit, they will receive an error message. To free up space, users can delete some resource groups or raise a ticket to increase their quota. [Data: Sources (3321), Date_Range ((2024, 03, 08), (2024, 03, 08))]\n\n## Permissions APIs Deprecation\n\nAll /v1/permissions APIs are deprecated and will be retired with the 2408a release. Users are required to migrate to use /v1/groups/{groupId}/users APIs. [Data: Sources (3322), Date_Range ((2024, 03, 07), (2024, 03, 07))]\n\n## Security Recommendations\n\nSecurity recommendations for the application router have been published. Users are advised to review the updated documentation for more information. [Data: Sources (3328), Date_Range ((2024, 03, 07), (2024, 03, 07))]", "# SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Environment Overview as of April 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of the SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry environment, highlighting key components, their relationships, and significant updates. The information is relevant to the SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry environment as of April 2025.\n\n## SAP Java Buildpack 1 Deprecation\n\nSAP Java Buildpack 1 has been deprecated and will be removed from the SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry environment in June 2025. This change is driven by the availability of SAP Java Buildpack 2, which provides support for the latest Java versions and Tomcat. The deprecation of SAP Java Buildpack 1 is crucial for maintaining the environment's stability and ensuring compliance with evolving market regulations. [Data: Sources (2368, 1116), Date_Range ((2024, 08, 16), (2025, 04, 03))]\n\n## SAP Alert Notification Service Updates\n\nThe SAP Alert Notification Service has been updated to support new database events, including HDB NSE Buffer Cache Unload Threshold and HDB Memory Usage. These updates enhance the service's capabilities and provide users with more information to manage their SAP HANA Cloud Service databases effectively. [Data: Sources (1117, 1118), Date_Range ((2025, 04, 03), (2025, 04, 03))]\n\n## SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Runtime Updates\n\nThe SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Runtime has been updated to version 48.4.0, which includes various improvements and bug fixes. This update enhances the runtime's stability and performance, ensuring a seamless experience for users. [Data: Sources (1118), Date_Range ((2025, 04, 03), (2025, 04, 03))]\n\n## SAP Mobile Start Availability\n\nSAP Mobile Start is now available as a mobile application for SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition, and SAP SuccessFactors Work Zone. This update provides users with a more convenient way to access business content and perform tasks on-the-go. [Data: Sources (1119), Date_Range ((2025, 04, 03), (2025, 04, 03))]\n\n## SAP Java Buildpack Updates\n\nSAP Java Buildpack 1 has been updated to version 1.111.0, which includes various component updates and improvements. This update enhances the buildpack's stability and performance, ensuring a seamless experience for users. [Data: Sources (1120), Date_Range ((2025, 03, 25), (2025, 04, 03))]", "# SAP BTP Cloud Foundry Runtime and Multitarget Applications Overview as of February 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP BTP Cloud Foundry Runtime and Multitarget Applications, highlighting key updates and changes as of February 2025. The information is relevant to the company's operations and maintenance of these services.\n\n## SAP BTP Cloud Foundry Runtime Updates\n\nSAP BTP Cloud Foundry Runtime has undergone several updates as of February 2025, including the replacement of the root certificate to comply with the latest recommendations from the German BSI on key-length for certificates and to ensure quantum-safe cryptography. This change is scheduled to take place in July 2025. Additionally, the service has been updated to provide Apache TomEE 10, Plume distribution, as part of the SAP Java Buildpack 2. These updates aim to enhance the security and stability of the service, ensuring it remains compliant with regulatory standards and continues to support the company's cloud-based services and applications effectively. [Data: Sources (1347, 1348), Date_Range ((2025, 02, 20), (2025, 07, 12))]\n\n## Multitarget Applications for Cloud Foundry Updates\n\nMultitarget Applications for Cloud Foundry has also undergone updates as of February 2025, including the change of the default service plan of the autoscaler resource type to standard. This change aims to ease the consumption of the free standard service plan, which is available by default in all BTP accounts, unlike the lite service plan, which is available only in trial accounts. These updates aim to enhance the usability and flexibility of the service, ensuring it remains aligned with the company's cloud-based services and applications. [Data: Sources (121, 1349), Date_Range ((2025, 02, 20), (2025, 07, 12))]\n\n## Deprecation of Endpoints and Themes\n\nSeveral endpoints and themes have been deprecated as of February 2025, including the Enrichment Data API endpoint Delete Enrichment Data (Synchronous), the Document API endpoint Get Request Payload, and the SAP Belize themes. These deprecations aim to improve security, compliance, and usability, ensuring the company's cloud-based services and applications remain stable, secure, and compliant with regulatory standards. [Data: Sources (1343, 1345, 1346), Date_Range ((2025, 02, 20), (2025, 07, 12))]", "# SAP Cloud Foundry and SAP BTP Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report delves into SAP's key components and services focusing on Cloud Foundry and SAP BTP, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to provide a comprehensive platform for application development and deployment. The information is relevant to SAP's operations around 2025.\n\n## Cloud Foundry and SAP BTP Integration\n\nCloud Foundry and SAP BTP are integrated to provide a comprehensive platform for application development and deployment. This integration enables developers to build, deploy, and manage applications on a single platform, streamlining the development process and improving efficiency. The integration also provides a unified view of applications, making it easier to manage and monitor them. [Data: Sources (120, 1347), Date_Range ((2025, 02, 20), (2025, 02, 24))]\n\n## SAP Build Process Automation and Cloud Foundry\n\nSAP Build Process Automation is integrated with Cloud Foundry to provide a seamless experience for developers. This integration enables developers to build and deploy processes on Cloud Foundry, making it easier to automate business processes and improve efficiency. The integration also provides a unified view of processes, making it easier to manage and monitor them. [Data: Sources (1341, 1343), Date_Range ((2025, 02, 20), (2025, 02, 24))]\n\n## SAP Task Center and Cloud Foundry\n\nSAP Task Center is integrated with Cloud Foundry to provide a comprehensive platform for task management. This integration enables developers to create, assign, and manage tasks on Cloud Foundry, making it easier to manage and monitor tasks. The integration also provides a unified view of tasks, making it easier to track progress and identify bottlenecks. [Data: Sources (2957, 2958), Date_Range ((2024, 05, 14), (2024, 05, 14))]", "# SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Runtime and Related Components Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report delves into the key components of SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Runtime, highlighting their interactions and updates within the organizational framework to ensure seamless operations and compliance with evolving market regulations. The information is relevant to the company's operations around 2025.\n\n## Root Certificate Replacement in SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Environment\n\nSAP is switching to the \"DigiCert TLS RSA4096 Root G5\" and \"DigiCert Global Root G3\" PKI in July 2025 to comply with the latest recommendations from the German BSI on the key-length for certificates and to ensure quantum-safe cryptography. This change aims to ensure a seamless transition for clients of applications offered by SAP and those operated by customers. [Data: Records (873, 1347), Date_Range ((2025, 02, 20), (2025, 07, 12))]\n\n## Cloud Foundry API v2 Deprecation and Removal\n\nThe Cloud Foundry API v2 is deprecated and replaced by the Cloud Foundry API v3. The usage of the Cloud Foundry API v2 is restricted by rate limits in the range of a few hundred requests per hour per user. Starting in April 2025, those limits will decrease over time and eventually reach zero in the first quarter of 2026. At that point, CF API v2 will not be available anymore. [Data: Records (871, 872), Date_Range ((2022, 07, 14), (2025, 05, 15))]\n\n## Feature Flags Service Updates\n\nThe Feature Flags Dashboard user interface is now upgraded to SAP Fiori, Horizon. Additionally, you can now share SAP Feature Flags service instances between different Cloud Foundry organizations in the same subaccount. [Data: Records (876, 877), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 07), (2025, 05, 15))]\n\n## Trading Partner Management Updates\n\nThe integration package Cloud Integration - Trading Partner Management V2 has been upgraded to version 2.1.0. With this update, a new integration flow supporting the ProcessDirect adapter has been added. Additionally, a new integration flow for writing the message to the message queue has been added. [Data: Records (4021, 4022), Date_Range ((2023, 10, 23), (2023, 10, 23))]\n\n## SAP Build Process Automation Updates\n\nA new set of 21 content packages, 13 Business Content and 8 Learning Content have been added to the Store during Sep-Oct 2023. These content packages are tailored to different lines of business such as IT, Sales, Services, Sourcing, Finance, and Procurement. [Data: Records (4026), Date_Range ((2023, 09, 01), (2023, 10, 31))]", "# SAP Technology Updates Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report delves into SAP's key technology updates, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to enhance operational efficiency and manage technological risks effectively. The information is relevant to SAP's operations around 2025.\n\n## SAP Business Application Studio Updates\n\nSAP Business Application Studio has undergone significant updates, including the introduction of new features such as the wizard-based runner and the ability to view and edit destinations. These updates aim to enhance the development experience and improve operational efficiency. Effective implementation of these updates can support SAP's strategic decision-making processes and ensure continuous compliance with evolving technological standards. [Data: Sources (162, 163), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 01, 26))]\n\n## PostgreSQL and Hyperscaler Option Updates\n\nPostgreSQL and Hyperscaler Option have undergone updates, including the end of life of version 12 and the introduction of new features such as on-demand backups. These updates aim to enhance operational efficiency and improve data management. Effective implementation of these updates can support SAP's strategic decision-making processes and ensure continuous compliance with evolving technological standards. [Data: Sources (167, 168), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 03, 06))]\n\n## Cloud Foundry Runtime Updates\n\nCloud Foundry Runtime has undergone updates, including the introduction of new features such as version 42.1.0 and version 48.0.0. These updates aim to enhance operational efficiency and improve data management. Effective implementation of these updates can support SAP's strategic decision-making processes and ensure continuous compliance with evolving technological standards. [Data: Sources (191, 192), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 03, 06))]", "# SAP Cloud Foundry and AI Core Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report delves into SAP's key components focusing on Cloud Foundry and AI Core, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to provide innovative solutions for data management, integration, and modeling. The information is relevant to SAP's operations around 2024.\n\n## Cloud Foundry Features and Updates\n\nCloud Foundry at SAP provides a robust platform for data management, integration, and modeling. Recent updates, such as the introduction of new features for data cataloging, data integration, and data modeling, have enhanced the platform's capabilities. These updates are crucial for supporting SAP's data-driven initiatives and ensuring seamless data management across various applications. [Data: Sources (704, 705), Date_Range ((2024, 11, 05), (2024, 11, 05))]\n\n## AI Core Capabilities and Enhancements\n\nSAP AI Core has been enhanced with new features, including the Generative AI hub, which provides a pipeline API for segmenting data into chunks and generating embeddings. This feature is essential for supporting SAP's AI-driven initiatives and enabling the development of more sophisticated AI models. [Data: Sources (1994, 1995), Date_Range ((2024, 11, 04), (2024, 11, 04))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Innovation\n\nCollaboration between the Cloud Foundry and AI Core teams has been instrumental in integrating data management and AI capabilities. This synergy has enabled the development of more innovative solutions and has been crucial for supporting SAP's data-driven initiatives. [Data: Sources (704, 1994), Date_Range ((2024, 11, 05), (2024, 11, 04))]", "# SAP BTP Technology Overview as of 2023\n\nThis report delves into SAP BTP's key components focusing on technology, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to uphold technological standards and manage system risks effectively. The information is relevant to the company's operations around 2023.\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Operational Scope\n\nThe Cloud Identity Services Department at SAP BTP plays a pivotal role in identifying, assessing, and mitigating technological risks. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2023, helps safeguard SAP BTP against potential technological pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective risk management not only prevents technological anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (541, 542), Date_Range ((2023, 01, 01), (2023, 10, 11))]\n\n## Kyma Runtime and Eventing Module\n\nThe Kyma Runtime and Eventing Module at SAP BTP ensure that all operations adhere to the technological standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on Eventing and NATS, noted starting Q2 2023, is crucial in maintaining SAP BTP's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex events and NATS configurations. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high technological standards and ethical practices. [Data: Source (3852), Date_Range ((2023, 04, 01), (2023, 11, 15))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between the various technology components, established in Q2 2023, ensures that technological risks are mitigated and that compliance measures consider financial risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating risk management with technological compliance strategies at SAP BTP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (4076, 4077), Date_Range ((2023, 04, 01), (2023, 10, 11))]", "# SAP BTP Technology Overview as of March 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP BTP's key technology components, highlighting their relationships and interactions within the organizational framework. The information is relevant to the company's operations around March 2025.\n\n## Integration Advisor Operational Scope\n\nThe Integration Advisor at SAP BTP plays a pivotal role in integrating various components and services. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2025, helps safeguard SAP BTP against potential integration pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective integration not only prevents operational anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (329), Date_Range ((2025, 03, 11), (2025, 03, 11))]\n\n## SAP Business Application Studio Development Experience\n\nThe SAP Business Application Studio at SAP BTP provides a comprehensive development experience, enabling developers to create and deploy applications efficiently. The studio's features, such as the Runtime Capabilities editor, have been updated to support various runtime capabilities, including Telemetry, Change Tracking, and Attachments. [Data: Sources (587, 1181), Date_Range ((2025, 03, 23), (2025, 03, 23))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between SAP BTP's technology components, such as the Integration Advisor and SAP Business Application Studio, ensures that integration strategies are compliant and that compliance measures consider technological advancements. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating SAP BTP's strategies with regulatory requirements. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with technological advancements. [Data: Sources (329, 1181), Date_Range ((2025, 03, 11), (2025, 03, 23))]", "# SAP BTP Technology Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP BTP's key technology components, highlighting their relationships and significance within the organizational framework. The information is relevant to SAP BTP's operations as of 2025.\n\n## SAP BTP Technology Components\n\nSAP BTP's technology components, including SAP Business Application Studio, Kyma Runtime, and Cloud Foundry, play a pivotal role in supporting the company's technological advancements. These components enable the development and deployment of cloud-based applications, ensuring seamless integration and scalability. Effective management of these components is crucial for maintaining SAP BTP's operational stability and competitiveness in the market. [Data: Sources (587, 588), Date_Range ((2025, 03, 20), (2025, 09, 19))]\n\n## Cloud Foundry Environment\n\nThe Cloud Foundry environment is a critical component of SAP BTP, enabling the deployment and management of cloud-based applications. The environment's scalability and flexibility make it an ideal choice for SAP BTP's operational needs. The addition of new regions, such as Europe (Frankfurt) - EU Access Only, further enhances the environment's capabilities. [Data: Sources (82, 83, 84), Date_Range ((2025, 09, 19), (2025, 09, 19))]\n\n## Kyma Runtime\n\nKyma Runtime is a key component of SAP BTP, enabling the development and deployment of cloud-native applications. The release of the Cloud Manager module further enhances the runtime's capabilities, allowing for more efficient management of cloud resources. Effective use of Kyma Runtime is crucial for SAP BTP's operational stability and competitiveness in the market. [Data: Sources (1181, 1182), Date_Range ((2025, 03, 20), (2025, 03, 20))]", "# SAP BTP Technology Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP BTP's key components and their relationships, highlighting their roles in ensuring the effective management of technology within the organization. The information is relevant to SAP BTP's operations around 2024.\n\n## Cloud Foundry Updates\n\nCloud Foundry has been updated from version 34.1.0 to 35.1.0, and from version 36.0.0 to 37.0.0, respectively. These updates aim to improve the platform's performance and security. The new version includes bug fixes and enhancements, such as the ability to configure a nodeSelector section for each pod related to the Connectivity Proxy. [Data: Sources (3612, 3395), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 25), (2024, 02, 22))]\n\n## SAP BTP Command Line Interface\n\nThe SAP BTP Command Line Interface (CLI) has been updated to version 2.38, which enables developers to access the REST APIs of the SAP Authorization and Trust Management service for all account types. Using the btp create security/api-credential command, developers can create API credentials, list available API credentials, display their details, and delete them. [Data: Source (3611), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 11), (2024, 01, 25))]\n\n## SAP Build Process Automation Enhancements\n\nSAP Build Process Automation has introduced several enhancements, including the ability to create environments in which projects can be deployed and run. This feature allows for improved security by restricting access to projects and monitoring, or for enabling the deployment of different project versions in different configurations. [Data: Sources (3613, 3614, 3615), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 25), (2024, 01, 25))]"], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small"}}, "key": "embeddings_2a4ca90956086fc314a4988978192560c308f1300d8101ff4ecd27f04666a2b8_v2"}